From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sun, 06 Sep 2026 01:20:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wayland_vulkan: build against Vulkan-Headers before 1.3.296

Vulkan-Headers 1.3.296 moved resultCheck and defaultDispatchLoaderDynamic from
VULKAN_HPP_NAMESPACE into VULKAN_HPP_NAMESPACE::detail. This source is written against
the post-move layout, so on an older header set both uses fail with

  error: 'vk::detail' has not been declared

AGL scarthgap ships Vulkan-Headers 1.3.275, and the copy vendored in this tree
(third_party/Vulkan-Headers, v1.3.292) is also pre-move -- and is not on the include path
in any case, because third_party/CMakeLists.txt adds Vulkan-Headers/include/vulkan while
the source includes "vulkan/vulkan.hpp", one level too deep to resolve. So the sysroot's
headers are what this actually compiles against.

Rather than move the call sites backwards, alias the pre-move names into vk::detail under
a VK_HEADER_VERSION guard. The call sites are then untouched, and the file still builds
unchanged once the distro's headers reach 1.3.296.

The alias must come after VULKAN_HPP_DEFAULT_DISPATCH_LOADER_DYNAMIC_STORAGE, which is
what declares the variable being aliased. VULKAN_HPP_DISPATCH_LOADER_DYNAMIC is already
forced to 1 by wayland_vulkan.h:25, so the dynamic dispatcher exists on both header
versions.

Upstream: not submitted. Local to the flutter-auto-vulkan recipe, which exists only to
measure the AGL instrument cluster on Vulkan against the same application on OpenGL.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [compatibility shim for Vulkan-Headers older than
 1.3.296; upstream builds against current headers and has no reason to carry it]
 A backward-compatibility guard for Vulkan-Headers older than 1.3.296, which is
 what AGL scarthgap ships (1.3.275). Upstream builds against a newer header set,
 so it has no reason to carry this; it has not been submitted.
---
 shell/backend/wayland_vulkan/wayland_vulkan.cc | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/shell/backend/wayland_vulkan/wayland_vulkan.cc b/shell/backend/wayland_vulkan/wayland_vulkan.cc
--- a/shell/backend/wayland_vulkan/wayland_vulkan.cc
+++ b/shell/backend/wayland_vulkan/wayland_vulkan.cc
@@ -26,6 +26,22 @@
 
 VULKAN_HPP_DEFAULT_DISPATCH_LOADER_DYNAMIC_STORAGE
 
+// Vulkan-Headers 1.3.296 moved resultCheck and defaultDispatchLoaderDynamic into
+// VULKAN_HPP_NAMESPACE::detail. The uses below are written against that layout; on the
+// 1.3.275 headers AGL scarthgap ships, both live at namespace scope and the compiler
+// reports "'vk::detail' has not been declared".
+//
+// Alias the pre-move names into vk::detail instead of rewriting the call sites, so this
+// file is correct on both header generations and needs no further change when the distro
+// catches up. This must follow the storage macro above: that is what declares
+// defaultDispatchLoaderDynamic.
+#if VK_HEADER_VERSION < 296
+namespace vk::detail {
+using VULKAN_HPP_NAMESPACE::defaultDispatchLoaderDynamic;
+using VULKAN_HPP_NAMESPACE::resultCheck;
+}  // namespace vk::detail
+#endif
+
 const auto& d = vk::detail::defaultDispatchLoaderDynamic;
 
 #define S1(x) #x
